---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import Content from "../components/Content.astro";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy · Bleep">
  <SiteHeader />
  <main
    class="max-w-160 mx-auto px-[var(--safe-area-padding)] pb-16 pt-[120px] md:pt-[140px]"
  >
    <Content>
      <h1 class="font-display font-normal text-2xl md:text-3xl pb-6">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>

      <p><em>Last updated: August 23, 2026</em></p>

      <p>
        At Bleep, we are committed to protecting your privacy and ensuring the
        security of your information. This Privacy Policy explains how we handle
        your private content and anonymous usage data in our iOS and macOS app.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Information Collection and Use</h2>

      <h3>Private Bleep Content</h3>
      <p>
        Bleep is designed so that we cannot access the content you create or
        save in the app. This includes your notes, saved links, images, files,
        room names, and search terms. Your content remains on your device and,
        if you enable iCloud sync, in your personal iCloud account. It is never
        included in Bleep's app analytics.
      </p>

      <h3>Anonymous App Analytics</h3>
      <p>
        We use TelemetryDeck, a privacy-focused analytics service provided by
        TelemetryDeck GmbH, to understand how Bleep is used and improve the app.
      </p>
      <p>
        Bleep sends limited usage events, such as when the app is launched or a
        feature is used, together with technical information such as the app and
        build version, operating system version, device type, language, locale,
        and region.
      </p>
      <p>
        These events are associated with an anonymized identifier that cannot be
        traced by us or TelemetryDeck to a particular person. TelemetryDeck
        hashes the identifier before it leaves the device and hashes it again on
        its servers. TelemetryDeck does not store IP addresses and does not use
        cookies, advertising identifiers, or technologies that track people
        across other companies' apps or websites.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not send TelemetryDeck your name, email address, Apple ID, precise
        location, contacts, or any of your private Bleep content, including
        notes, links, images, files, room names, or search terms. We do not sell
        analytics data or use it for targeted advertising.
      </p>
      <p>
        TelemetryDeck processes anonymous event data on infrastructure located
        in Europe. Events are available to us for the analytics retention period
        included with our TelemetryDeck service. Older anonymous events may
        remain in TelemetryDeck's cold storage. Because events are not
        associated with your identity, neither Bleep nor TelemetryDeck can
        locate analytics events belonging to a particular person.
      </p>
      <p>
        Anonymous app analytics are collected automatically when you use Bleep.
        Because the events cannot be associated with your identity, they cannot
        be accessed or deleted on an individual basis. For more information,
        review TelemetryDeck's <a
          href="https://telemetrydeck.com/docs/guides/privacy-faq/"
          >Privacy FAQ</a
        > and <a href="https://telemetrydeck.com/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Data Storage and Sync</h2>

      <h3>Local Storage</h3>
      <p>
        Your private Bleep content is primarily stored locally on your device.
        This means that your content remains under your control at all times.
      </p>

      <h3>iCloud Sync</h3>
      <p>
        To provide seamless synchronization between your devices, Bleep uses
        Apple's iCloud service. When you enable iCloud sync:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Your Bleep data is encrypted and securely stored in your personal
          iCloud account.
        </li>
        <li>The sync process is managed entirely by Apple's iCloud service.</li>
        <li>
          We do not have access to your iCloud account or the data stored within
          it.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Please note that the use of iCloud is subject to Apple's own terms of
        service and privacy policy. We encourage you to review Apple's privacy
        practices for more information on how they handle your data.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Data Security</h2>

      <p>
        We take reasonable measures to help protect your data within the Bleep
        app:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Your private Bleep content is stored locally on your device, protected
          by your device's built-in security features.
        </li>
        <li>
          When using iCloud sync, your data is protected by Apple's encryption
          standards during transmission and storage.
        </li>
        <li>
          We recommend using strong device passcodes and enabling biometric
          authentication (like Face ID or Touch ID) for additional security.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Service Providers</h2>

      <p>
        Bleep does not share your private content with third-party services. We
        use Apple's iCloud for optional data synchronization and TelemetryDeck
        for the anonymous app analytics described above. TelemetryDeck does not
        receive your private Bleep content or information that directly
        identifies you.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Children's Privacy</h2>

      <p>
        Bleep is not directed to children under the age of 13. We do not
        knowingly collect or maintain personal information from children under
        13. Anonymous app analytics cannot be associated with a particular child
        or other individual.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>

      <p>
        We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you
        of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy in the app and updating
        the "Last updated" date at the top of this policy.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your Choices and Rights</h2>

      <p>
        You have control over your private Bleep content, which is stored
        locally or in your personal iCloud account. You can view, edit, or
        delete that content within the app. Anonymous analytics events are not
        associated with your identity, so they cannot be retrieved or deleted
        for a particular person.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Contact Us</h2>

      <p>
        If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us
        at <a href="mailto:privacy@bleep.is">privacy@bleep.is</a>.
      </p>

      <p>Bleep LLC</p>
    </Content>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>
